//@version=6
// =============================================================================
//  ZoneEngineV2_Rebuild
//  Zone definition spec v2 + lightweight implementation instructions (appendix
//  A-D, M0-M19) are the only normative sources. Zone logic is unchanged; the
//  data structures and the evaluation order are built for runtime and memory.
//
//  Build ID .......... ZEV2R-20260919-006
//  Base timeframe .... confirmed 5m bar, engine updates exactly once per bar
//
//  Layering (M3). State transition never runs after candidate evaluation:
//    Source/Feed      -> helper packs evaluated in their own request context
//    Root registry    -> id/slot split, origin + category indices
//    Candidate eval   -> stage A dense point cores, stage B FVG candidates
//                        (local point roots inside an FVG, Proximal
//                        localisation, same-direction overlap, standalone,
//                        Broad context), stage C normal candidates
//    Core association -> identity / merge / split / pending topology
//    State transition -> touch / weak / break / flip / reclaim / inverse
//    Read API         -> views + events, read-only projections
//    Presentation     -> harness only, never feeds back into logic
// =============================================================================
library("ZoneEngineV2_Rebuild", overlay = true)

export buildId() =>
    "ZEV2R-20260919-006"

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Constants (int codes only; strings are produced at presentation time)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
